# 🤝 Behavioral Question

## Question

**How do you approach troubleshooting an unfamiliar IT problem?**

### Answer

> I start by gathering information and asking appropriate questions to understand the issue. Based on the user's responses, I identify possible causes and begin with basic troubleshooting steps. I make changes only when I understand the cause and am authorized to make the change. After making a change, I verify the result with the user. If the issue remains unresolved or requires higher-level access, I document everything I have tried and escalate the issue appropriately.

